          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Does a bigger tank waste energy?</h3>

          <p>
            Not in any meaningful way, and it usually helps. A larger tank gives the heat pump more time to work before the resistance elements are needed, and those elements are where most of the savings leak away. Standby loss climbs slightly with tank size, but on a well-insulated modern tank that is small next to the gain from avoiding resistance heat.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Should you size for the future?</h3>

          <p>
            Yes. If teenagers are on the way or guests stay often, size for the busier household ahead. A heat pump water heater is a 10 to 15 year purchase, and trading it in early for a bigger one costs far more than buying the right size at the start.
          </p>
