          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            9. How Much Does It Cost to Install a Heat Pump Water Heater?
          </h2>

          <p>
            At the time of writing, swapping an electric resistance tank for a 240-volt hybrid often runs roughly $3,000 to $5,000 including the unit. A gas-to-heat-pump conversion that needs a new circuit can run higher, a 120-volt plug-in can shrink or remove the electrical portion, and split systems typically cost significantly more.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What does the installation involve?</h3>

          <p>
            The same water connections, relief valve and expansion tank work as any tank, plus a condensate drain and, for a 240-volt model, a dedicated circuit. Replacing an electric tank in a roomy basement is often straightforward. Replacing a gas tank adds removing the gas line and venting, and possibly new electrical work, which pushes the cost up. Many jurisdictions require permits for both the plumbing and the electrical work.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Is there still a federal tax credit?</h3>

          <p>
            Not for new installs. The 25C tax credit, which used to cover 30 percent of the cost of a qualifying heat pump water heater up to $2,000, was ended by 2025 federal legislation for equipment placed in service after December 31, 2025. Confirm the current rules with a tax professional before counting on any federal benefit. State rebate programs funded under earlier federal law, and utility rebates, may still be available depending on where you live.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why plan the swap before the old tank fails?</h3>

          <p>
            A failed tank forces a rushed decision, and the installer may only have conventional tanks on the truck. Collecting quotes ahead of time, checking rebate programs and confirming electrical capacity lets you make the switch on your own schedule.
          </p>

